<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-HERMIS SEES HIGHER 97 PROFIT, TO PAY 96 DIV.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-HERMIS SEES HIGHER 97 PROFIT, TO PAY 96 DIV.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's Hermis Bank said on Friday that it was to pay a 3.5 litas per share 1996 dividend and expected its 1997 profit to rise to 40.6 million litas.</p>
<p>Chairman Nadezhda Novickiene also told a news conference that the dividend for preference shares, which are held only by the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), would be 50 litas per share.</p>
</text>
